# kraken2 software prefetch: batched minimizer lookups (-B)
#
# WHAT
#   Splits the classification inner loop into two passes. Pass 1 scans B
#   minimizers, hashes each once, and issues __builtin_prefetch for the hash
#   table line it will land on -- without waiting. Pass 2 resolves them in the
#   original order, by which time the lines have arrived. The same memory
#   accesses happen; they simply overlap instead of queueing.
#
#   New flag:  -B NUM   batch size, 1..64.  Default 1 = the stock code path.
#
# APPLIES TO
#   This project's FORKED tree (kraken2/src, git 7c0eb91, which already carries
#   the 16/20/24/40-bit cell-size work) -- NOT upstream kraken2 2.17.1.
#
#     cd kraken2 && patch -p1 < ../scripts/kraken2_prefetch.patch
#
# MEASURED (pod5_2, 151591 reads / 499.98 Mbp / 160,625,038 lookups,
#           eskape_32bit_fork, -p 16 -g 2 -T 0, mean of 3 interleaved reps)
#   stock   2.893 s   IPC 1.13   0.938 DRAM accesses/lookup
#   -B 4    2.572 s   IPC 1.35   0.142   (nearly all the memory benefit)
#   -B 29   2.553 s   IPC 1.49   0.141   -11.77% vs stock, best measured
#   Curve is flat by 32. Instructions rise ~11%; cycles fall ~15%.
#
# CORRECTNESS
#   Output file AND report byte-identical to stock kraken2_bin/classify at
#   -B 1/8/16/32 x -p 1/16 x pod5_15/pod5_2 -- 16 of 16 exact.
#
# FRAGILE DEPENDENCY -- read before editing
#   In pass 2, add_kmer() uses the captured pf[i].min instead of
#   scanner.last_minimizer(), because the scanner has advanced past the batch.
#   That substitution is only valid because NextMinimizer() returns
#   &last_minimizer_ (mmscanner.cc:146,156,188). If upstream ever changes what
#   NextMinimizer() returns, this breaks SILENTLY -- wrong report counts, no
#   compile error. Same reason scanner.is_ambiguous() is captured per entry.
#
# DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED
#   The depth-1 last_minimizer/last_taxon skip; minimizer_hit_groups++ and its
#   position; hit_counts; taxa.push_back ordering; the quick_mode goto.
#   (An earlier patch in this project moved that increment and silently changed
#   hit-group counts at frame boundaries.)
#
